# `DfoBuilder::with_constraints_values`

[Back to `dfo::DfoBuilder`](../DfoBuilder.md)

Sets inequality and equality constraints through `DfoConstraintValues`.

## Signature

```cpp
dfo::DfoBuilder dfo::DfoBuilder::with_constraints_values(std::function<dfo::DfoConstraintValues(const pluss::Series &)> constraints_values) const;
template <class Fn> dfo::DfoBuilder dfo::DfoBuilder::with_constraints_values(Fn &&constraints_values) const;
```

## What It Does

The callable returns a [`DfoConstraintValues`](../DfoConstraintValues.md) with an `inequality` part (`≤ 0`) and an `equality` part (`= 0`). A callable that returns a plain `Series` or number is taken as inequality values. Equality constraints are supported by pattern search, the method the front door chooses for constrained problems.

## Parameters

`std::function<dfo::DfoConstraintValues(const pluss::Series &)> constraints_values`
: The constraint values.

## Returns

A new builder with the change; the original is untouched.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

An equality constraint. Minimise `Σ (xᵢ − 3)²` on the line `x₀ + x₁ = 2`: the answer is `(1, 1)`.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(3));
  const auto f = [](const Series &x) { return (x - 3.0).square().sum(); };   // minimum 0 at (3, 3)

  const dfo::DfoResult r = dfo::DFO::build(pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0})).with_objective(f).with_constraints_values([](const Series &x) {
    dfo::DfoConstraintValues c;
    c.equality = x.sum() - 2.0;
    return c;
  }).solve();
  out.writeln("minimizer =", r.minimizer.items<double>(), ", violation =", r.diagnostics.max_constraint_violation);
}
```

### Example 2

Both kinds: the line `x₀ − x₁ = 0` and the half-plane `x₀ + x₁ ≤ 4`. The answer is `(2, 2)`.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(3));
  const auto f = [](const Series &x) { return (x - 3.0).square().sum(); };   // minimum 0 at (3, 3)

  const dfo::DfoResult r = dfo::DFO::build(pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0})).with_objective(f).with_constraints_values([](const Series &x) {
    dfo::DfoConstraintValues c;
    c.inequality = x.sum() - 4.0;
    c.equality = x.select(0, 0) - x.select(0, 1);
    return c;
  }).solve();
  out.writeln("minimizer =", r.minimizer.items<double>());
}
```

### Example 3

A callable that returns a Series is read as inequality values.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(3));
  const auto f = [](const Series &x) { return (x - 3.0).square().sum(); };   // minimum 0 at (3, 3)

  const dfo::DfoResult r = dfo::DFO::build(pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0})).with_objective(f).with_constraints_values([](const Series &x) { return x.sum() - 2.0; }).solve();
  out.writeln("minimizer =", r.minimizer.items<double>());
}
```

